<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boston Tea Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1773">1773</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">Tea</a> Party was a political protest on 16 December 1773 in which American colonists, some disguised as Mohawk Indians, threw 342 chests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> tea into Boston Harbor in defiance of the Tea Act. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> answered with the punitive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intolerable-acts">Coercive Acts</a> of 1774, which hardened colonial resistance and led towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston-tea-party.jpg" alt="Boston Tea Party" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Cornischong at lb.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boston_Tea_Party_w.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
